>> title: Chocolate Chip Cookies
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: chocolate, butter, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Deli
>> aka: choc chip cookies, Toll House cookies
>> pairs-with: french-vanilla-ice-cream
>> servings: 48
>> time: 30 min

Heat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

>> step: cream
Cream @unsalted butter{1%cup}(226 g; softened) with @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g) and @light brown sugar{3/4%cup}(165 g).

>> step: beat in
Beat @eggs{2%large}(100 g) and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2 1/4%cup}(280 g), @baking soda{1%tsp}(6 g), and @table salt{1%tsp}(6 g).

Stir @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)batter{}.

Fold @semisweet chocolate chips{2%cup}(340 g) into @&(~1)dough{}.

Bake @&(~1)dough{} in rounded spoonfuls at 375°F for ~{10%min}.
